| G1      | Fulfill Mission | Achieve | Mission completed successfully | -         | Top-level goal |
| G1.1    | Collect Resources | Perform | Resources collected | AND       | Both collection phases must be completed |
| G1.1.1  | Navigate to Storage | Perform | Navigation successful | AND       | Sequential navigation |
| G1.1.2  | Request Resources | Perform | Resources requested | AND       | Sequential request |
| G1.1.3  | Handle Low Battery | Perform | Battery recharged | AND       | Sequential handling |
| G1.2    | Deliver Resources | Perform | Delivery completed | AND       | Both delivery phases must be completed |
| G1.2.1  | Navigate to Delivery | Perform | Navigation successful | AND       | Sequential navigation |
| G1.2.2  | Deliver Resources | Perform | Delivery completed | AND       | Sequential delivery |
| G1.2.3  | Handle Low Battery | Perform | Battery recharged | AND       | Sequential handling |

### Task Table

| Task ID | Task Title | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT1.1   | Navigate to Storage | Various locations | 1               | Sequential navigation |
| AT1.2   | Request Resources | Storage location | 1               | Single request per storage |
| AT1.3   | Recharge Battery | Recharging station | 1               | Battery management |
| AT2.1   | Navigate to Delivery | Delivery location | 1               | Sequential navigation |
| AT2.2   | Deliver Resources | Delivery location | 1               | Sequential delivery |
| AT2.3   | Return to Checkpoint | Checkpoint | 1               | Battery management |

This structure ensures that each phase of the mission is broken down into manageable tasks, with appropriate decomposition and justifications based on the mission requirements.
